### The Operating Leverage Thesis

The financial logic of this opportunity hinges on operating leverage — a structural feature well-documented in LTS's financials. Statistical analysis confirms that COGS has a trend strength (R²) of 0.652, meaning costs rise predictably but at a lower rate than revenue growth [23]. In Q1 2026, LTS achieved a 59.3% gross margin and 46.7% EBITDA margin on revenue that accelerated from $5.44M in January to $9.26M in March [26]. This confirms that as utilization increases, a disproportionate share of incremental revenue flows to profit.

